+# Blocked Task Resume Implementation Plan
+
+**Goal:** Recover the original blocked task without recreating work, losing progress, clearing send locks, or claiming that authentication restored email delivery.
+
+**Architecture:** Add a same-executor, evidence-referenced resume transition to the existing revision-CAS task store. Expose it through authenticated MCP and native browser tools. Keep channel verification, dispatch authorization and unknown-send reconciliation separate. Honor explicit no-resend/history flags in research-cache deduplication.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Existing JavaScript modules, SQLite/D1 adapter, Node test runner, native browser WebMCP.
+
+## 1. Reproduce and protect the failure
+
+- Add `tests/blocked-task-resume.test.mjs`; confirm the old implementation rejects all blocked-to-running recovery.
+- Cover preserved receipts, count, original executor, startedAt, channel states and send locks; deny terminal/foreign/concurrent takeover.
+- Replay one recovery reference idempotently; require a new reference after a later block.
+
+## 2. Minimal transition and tool wiring
+
+- Update `server/development-tasks.mjs`: bounded reference, original-executor ownership, single-running-task rule, original CAS write, resumed audit, no bridge redelivery.
+- Update `server/task-mcp.mjs` and `web/workspace-premium.js`: expose `resume_development_task`; MCP pins its executor. This records parent-task recovery, not successful channel authentication or any send.
+- Update `web/outreach-efficiency.js`: cached explicit permanent no-resend/history flags must not become eligible merely because a new research source appears.
+
+## 3. Verify and publish
+
+- Run new and related queue, resilience, browser/login, reload and efficiency regressions using bundled Node; run diff checks and one build.
+- Independently review changed authorization, replay, concurrency and lock paths.
+- Publish the unchanged tested archive to the existing private Site; verify deployment and actual authenticated UI/tool registration without mutating a production task.
+- Sync only generic safe repair code and anonymous statistics to the verified public GitHub repository; verify remote SHA. Keep customer identities and inquiry evidence local/private.
+
+## Acceptance boundaries
+
+- No real customer task is created just to test recovery; no mail, social message, credentials, DNS or security settings are changed by this repair.
+- Current live queue has no production blocked task. This fixes a reproduced future recovery dead end; it does not prove that this dead end caused the current outreach slowdown.
+- Remote email delivery and an unattended host executor remain separately unverified; no claim that this change connects either.
